---
description: Answer the requested local execution question and compose only requested evidence-bound handoffs.
args:
  goal: string
returns: LocalWidthOutcome
---
Own the user's actual capacity or current-state question. Use investigateLocalWidth to acquire and interpret relevant scoped native evidence. Choose further inquiries from the goal and their actual results; independent reads can run concurrently. A model listing, selectable provider, running server, advertised slot count and demonstrated completed overlap are different facts. Do not infer one from another or silently substitute a model the user requires exactly.

Return the grounded finding and explanation. If the user requests a retained note, decide whether the stated condition actually holds before using stageWidth. shouldRetainWidth can interpret that obligation; native release is only permission, never a request. Consume the actual stage result and report an unavailable or refused note honestly. A retained note does not replace a requested answer. Do not start, install or reconfigure anything through this read-only evidence interface. Preserve the exact machine, boot, configuration and protected workspace.
